  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through Monday)\nIssued at 244 AM EDT Tue Oct 20 2026\n\nDry and Mild Weather Continues:\n\nGuidance remains in good agreement on the forecast through the \nupcoming weekend, with a ridge over the South-Central US and \ntroughing over East Coast. North and Central GA will remain dry in \nthis setup, as primarily northerly flow keeps PWATs below 0.5\" and \nrain chances near zero. High temperatures on Thursday will remain a \nbit above normal, with mid to upper 70s for most. A reinforcing \nshortwave within the East Coast trough will drop across the area on \nFriday, with a slightly cooler airmass moving in for the weekend \nresulting in highs in the low 70s. Low temperatures will be fairly \nconsistent through this period, falling to the mid to upper 40s each \nnight.",
